  "answer": "This is a storefront discount bug. I'll follow the bug-fix playbook and start by reading its steps and the principles it depends on.The admin inventory mapper stores the special end date on the start-date field, and the price calculator then rejects a ranged special. I'll lock that in with a failing test before changing either path.A special price with an end date never reached the storefront. `PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper` wrote that end date into the start-date field, and `ProductPriceUtils` then required the start date to be both before and after today, so the discount was dropped whether or not a start date was also sent. Both now keep the end date and treat it as the end of the window. Fix Root Causes kept the change on those two lines. Test Behavior, Not Implementation and Prove It Works covered the stored dates and the discounted final price. Sequence work into verifiable units put the failing tests in the commit before the fix.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialDateTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\", \"mvn -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=PersistableProductAvailabilitySpecialDateTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\", \"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialDateTest,PersistableProductAvailabilitySpecialDateTest -DfailIfNoTests=false test\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": \"No live admin create followed by a storefront product read. The first two Maven runs failed on the new tests before the fix. The third run passed, 3 tests in sm-core and 2 in sm-shop.\", \"missing\": \"A documented HTTP fixture that creates a product with a dated special and reads the storefront price.\"}",
